"""X-MFG-34 in-house RO/EDI polish for BMED_UPW_POLISH (AQS-DUTY-070, A-M-176). Sized from the graph duty.
The feed S25 is VCD distillate. The potable share to REMIN does not need polishing and bypasses the train; only the UPW products
(IA-UPW-FAB to the fab, S01 to HDR_UPW) pass RO then EDI. RO: solution-diffusion J = A (dP - d pi), pi = 2 c R T [BAKER2012];
area = permeate / design flux; recovery from the reject edge on the graph. EDI: current I = F n / CE for the salt left in the RO permeate,
voltage per cell pair from the stack [ALVARADO2014]. Pump power Q dP / eta. Two RO modules and two EDI stacks (one standby) per the redundancy rule.
Run: python3 -m flow_graph.param.upw_polish [--write]"""
import json, math, os, sys
from . import drivers as DR
ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))))
GP = os.path.join(ROOT, 'flow_graph/plant_flow_graph.json')
def design(d, g):
    v = lambda k: DR.val(d, k); E = {e['stream_id']: e for e in g['edges']}; r = lambda k: float(E[k]['rate']['value'] or 0)
    upw = r('IA-UPW-FAB') + r('S01'); rej = r('IA-UPW-REJ'); feed = upw + rej; rec = upw/feed
    c = v('ro_feed_TDS_mg_L')/58.44                                                   # mol/m3 NaCl
    c_conc = c*(1 - (1 - v('ro_rejection'))*rec)/(1 - rec)                            # concentrate
    pi = 2*(c + c_conc)/2*8.314*v('WTR.potable-upw-train.BMED_UPW_POLISH.ro_eval_T_K')/1e5                                    # bar, mean feed-side
    dP = v('ro_flux_LMH')/v('ro_A_LMH_bar') + pi
    area = upw/24/v('ro_flux_LMH')                                                   # m2 (kg/d ~ L/d)
    Qf = feed/1000/86400; P_ro = Qf*dP*1e5/v('ro_pump_eta')/1000
    c_perm = c*(1 - v('ro_rejection')); n = upw/1000/86400*c_perm                    # mol/s
    I = 96485*n/v('edi_CE'); P_edi = I*v('edi_V_cell')*v('edi_cells')/1000
    P_uv = v('upw_uv_W')/1000
    return dict(UPW_kg_d=upw, bypass_kg_d=r('IA-UPW-REMIN'), RO_feed_kg_d=feed, recovery=rec, osmotic_bar=pi, feed_bar=dP, membrane_m2=area,
                modules=v('WTR.potable-upw-train.BMED_UPW_POLISH.ro_modules'), RO_kW=P_ro, EDI_A=I, EDI_kW=P_edi, UV_kW=P_uv, total_kW=P_ro + P_edi + P_uv,
                kWh_per_m3=(P_ro + P_edi + P_uv)*24/(feed/1000), kWh_per_m3_RO_EDI=(P_ro + P_edi)*24/(feed/1000))
def write(g, r):
    N = {n['unit_id']: n for n in g['nodes']}; E = {e['stream_id']: e for e in g['edges']}; n = N['BMED_UPW_POLISH']; TAG = 'X-MFG-34 (A-M-176, AQS-DUTY-070)'
    n['continuous_kw'] = {'value': round(r['total_kW'], 4), 'unit': 'kW', 'status': 'study', 'note': f"{TAG}: RO pump {r['RO_kW']*1000:.1f} W + EDI {r['EDI_kW']*1000:.2f} W + UV {r['UV_kW']*1000:.0f} W; potable share bypasses."}
    n['params']['internals'] = 'potable bypass; 2 x flat-sheet RO module, 2 x EDI stack, UV-TOC lamp'
    n['params']['design'] = json.loads(json.dumps(r, default=float))
    for sid in ('SF-BMED_UPW_POLISH', 'SQ-BMED_UPW_POLISH'):   # R11 Rev AC regen: SQ-* heat edges died with HEAT_SINK in Rev AC; update what exists
        if sid in E: E[sid]['rate']['value'] = round(r['total_kW'], 4)
    open(GP, 'w').write(json.dumps(g, indent=2))
    d = DR.load(); v = lambda k: DR.val(d, k); mods = v('WTR.potable-upw-train.BMED_UPW_POLISH.ro_modules')
    md = ['# Ultrapure water polish (RO and EDI)', '', 'Document number: AQS-DUTY-070', 'Revision: B', 'Date: 2026-10-29',
          'Generated by `flow_graph/param/upw_polish.py` from the plant graph and `flow_graph/param/drivers.json`. Do not edit by hand; change the generator or its inputs and run `python3 -m flow_graph.param.regen`.',
          'Authority: task X-MFG-34 of AQS-PLAN-007; assumption A-M-176. Study. Not a PE stamp.', '',
          '| Rev | Description | Date |', '| --- | --- | --- |',
          '| A | First issue: reverse osmosis and electrodeionisation sized from the graph duty; the potable share bypasses the train | 2026-10-16 |',
          '| B | Record of revisions, purpose and scope added; the design written as sentences with the driver values; tables numbered | 2026-10-29 |', '',
          '## 1. Purpose and scope', '',
          'This page sizes the ultrapure water (UPW) polish `BMED_UPW_POLISH`: a reverse osmosis (RO) stage, an electrodeionisation (EDI) stage and an ultraviolet lamp that destroys total organic carbon (UV-TOC). The flows come from the plant graph.', '',
          '## 2. Flows', '',
          f"The feed, stream S25, is distillate from the vapour compression distiller, with about {v('ro_feed_TDS_mg_L'):.0f} mg/L of dissolved solids (A-M-176). "
          f"The potable share of {r['bypass_kg_d']:.1f} kg/d goes to remineralisation `REMIN` and bypasses the polish. "
          f"The ultrapure water product of {r['UPW_kg_d']:.1f} kg/d, for the fab and the header `HDR_UPW`, passes through the RO stage and then the EDI stage. "
          f"The RO feed is {r['RO_feed_kg_d']:.1f} kg/d at a recovery of {r['recovery']*100:.1f} %; the reject leaves by stream IA-UPW-REJ.", '',
          '## 3. Design', '',
          f"The RO flux follows the solution-diffusion model J = A (ΔP − Δπ) [BAKER2012], with a permeance A of {v('ro_A_LMH_bar'):g} L/(m2 h bar) and a design flux of {v('ro_flux_LMH'):g} L/(m2 h). "
          f"This gives {r['membrane_m2']:.2f} m2 of flat-sheet thin-film composite membrane per module; {mods:g} modules are fitted, one of them standby. The mean osmotic pressure is {r['osmotic_bar']*1000:.0f} mbar and the feed pressure {r['feed_bar']:.1f} bar.",
          f"The EDI current carries the salt left in the RO permeate at a current efficiency of {v('edi_CE'):g}, through {v('edi_cells'):g} cell pairs at {v('edi_V_cell'):g} V each [ALVARADO2014]. Two stacks are fitted, one of them standby.",
          f"The UV-TOC lamp, at 185 nm and 254 nm on the ultrapure water loop, is rated {r['UV_kW']*1000:.0f} W (driver `upw_uv_W`).", '',
          'Table 3.1 gives the power of each stage.', '', 'Table 3.1. Power', '',
          '| Stage | Current or flow | Power (W) |', '|---|---|---|',
          f"| RO pump | {r['RO_feed_kg_d']:.1f} kg/d at {r['feed_bar']:.1f} bar | {r['RO_kW']*1000:.1f} |",
          f"| EDI | {r['EDI_A']*1000:.0f} mA | {r['EDI_kW']*1000:.2f} |",
          f"| UV-TOC | | {r['UV_kW']*1000:.0f} |",
          f"| Total | | {r['total_kW']*1000:.1f} |", '',
          f"The RO and EDI stages use {r['kWh_per_m3_RO_EDI']:.2f} kWh per cubic metre of RO feed, at the low end of the 0.5 to 3 kWh/m3 range for brackish water RO [GREENLEE2009], because distillate needs little pressure. With the UV lamp the figure is {r['kWh_per_m3']:.2f} kWh/m3.",
          'The permeance, the feed dissolved solids and the EDI current efficiency are assumptions until the modules are tested on the bench (A-M-176).']
    open(os.path.join(ROOT, 'docs-authority/sizing/UPW_POLISH.md'), 'w').write('\n'.join(md) + '\n')
def main():
    d = DR.load(); g = json.load(open(GP)); r = design(d, g); print(json.dumps(r, default=float))
    if '--write' in sys.argv: write(g, r)
if __name__ == '__main__': main()
